# =============================================================================
# .gitignore — my-trading-system
# =============================================================================
# Architecture: Python (blue_engine) -> OpenAlgo (server) -> Broker -> Exchange
#
# THE RULE: this repository contains YOUR CODE ONLY.
#
#   TRACKED    src/ (quant + blue_engine), scripts/, Servers/, patches/, README.md, .env.example
#   NEVER      openalgo/ (upstream - the installer clones it), _restored/ (secrets),
#              archive/ (retired code and backups), data/ (runtime ledger)
#
# If a secret ever reaches a commit, rotating the key is the ONLY fix. Removing
# the file in a later commit does not remove it from history.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRETS AND LOCAL STATE — never commit, ever
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# _restored/ holds .env AND db/. The .env carries FERNET_SALT and
# API_KEY_PEPPER, which are the KDF inputs that encrypt the broker session
# tokens stored in db/openalgo.db. Both are credentials.
_restored/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Databases — encrypted broker tokens, positions, order history
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Key material
keys/
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx

# Convenience copies of any of the above
deploy_*/
mts-state/
*_env_*
*_db_*

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# UPSTREAM PLATFORM — cloned by the installer, never tracked here
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tracking openalgo/ would either duplicate 3,175 files or create a submodule
# that `git pull` fights on every upgrade. Servers/install_ubuntu.sh clones it.
openalgo/
openalgo_new/
openalgo_fresh/
openalgo_OLD_*/
openalgo_retired_*/
# Same rule for the vendored screener-india clone: tracking it would duplicate
# the upstream TypeScript and fight `git pull`. It is NOT a runtime dependency
# either - src/quant/blue_engine/screener/client/ is the Python port that runs.
# Only the clone plus its pin file are kept in-tree; _vendor_pin.py
# --update-pin refreshes it. See src/quant/blue_engine/screener/README.md.
src/quant/blue_engine/screener/vendor/screener-india/
# The database research upstream is kept pristine and sparse; only its pin and
# our upgrade helper are tracked, never the upstream data/code checkout.
src/quant/blue_engine/database/vendor/indian-market-historical-data/
# Screener RUNTIME artifacts: the page cache is a local scraper cache, and
# last_screen.json is a per-run snapshot. Neither belongs in history.
src/quant/blue_engine/screener/cache/
src/quant/blue_engine/screener/last_screen.json
# Downloaded historical research data; sourced under non-commercial-only terms.
src/quant/blue_engine/database/sample_data/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RETIRED CODE AND BACKUPS — reference only, large, not needed on the VPS
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
archive/
_backup/
_retired_*/
_venv_hold/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RUNTIME STATE AND LOGS
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local cache only. Anchored so source packages named data/ stay tracked.
/data/
log/
logs/
*.log
*.out
*.err
tmp/
*.tmp

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PYTHON
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
.python-version
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
pip-wheel-metadata/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ENGINE RUNTIME ARTIFACTS
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
src/quant/blue_engine/input/*.local.json
src/quant/blue_engine/**/state.json
src/quant/blue_engine/**/*.jsonl

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TOOLING AND EDITORS
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SCRATCH / DIAGNOSTIC SCRIPTS
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ad-hoc probes and scanners. These have historically contained a literal API
# key inside their regex patterns, so they are excluded by default. Put real
# tools in scripts/ with a proper name rather than an underscore prefix.
scripts/_*.ps1
scripts/_*.py
_diag.ps1
move_log.txt

# Temp/ is the designated STAGING workspace (see AGENTS.md): research,
# experiments, downloaded docs, diagnostic probes. It is deliberately NOT
# tracked, for two reasons:
#   1. it is scratch by definition - a probe answers one question and is then
#      obsolete, and committing it turns the repo into a junk drawer;
#   2. the probes are run against real data and so are a place a credential can
#      leak by accident (a tqdm bar echoing a URL, a repr of a config object).
# Nothing in this repo imports from Temp/ except the OpenAlgo SDK submodule below.
# A probe worth keeping belongs in docs/ (its findings) or scripts/ (its code).
#
# Layout since 2026-10-21: Temp/ holds ONLY live staging work. Loose files are
# swept into Temp/archive/<YYYY-MM-DD>/<category>/ by
# Temp/Staging Workspace/archive_temp.py, which writes an index.txt recording
# every former path - so the root stays readable and nothing must be deleted.
Temp/*
# Exception: the OpenAlgo Python SDK is tracked as a submodule (pinned to v2.0.3)
# so the test suite can import it. Everything else in Temp/ stays ignored.
!Temp/openalgo-python-library/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EXCEPTIONS — things that look ignored but must be tracked
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
!.env.example
!src/quant/blue_engine/input/master.json
!src/quant/blue_engine/pyproject.toml
# Deployment config with the API key - the .example template IS tracked
Servers/deploy.env


# Agent working memory (runtime artifact, never a trading input)
_memory/
